## What Gravix guarantees

Containment of failure, not containment of intent. This plugin runs as a
subprocess with whatever network and filesystem access the operating system
grants it.

| Property | Rule |
|---|---|
| Timeout | 30s per call by default, then the process is killed |
| Crash | Restarted with exponential backoff up to 5 minutes |
| Failure budget | 5 consecutive failures disable it; it never blocks the pipeline |
| Memory | 256 MB RSS by default |

## Four things that will bite you

1. Flush after every response — a buffered response looks like a hang.
2. One JSON object per line; a pretty-printed response will not parse.
3. Never write anything but responses to stdout. Diagnostics go to stderr.
4. Return JSON-RPC errors rather than exiting. Exiting counts as a crash.

